JE","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"National holiday","content":"Liberation Day, 9 May (1945)","ordinal":44,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/je.html#field:44","country":"JE","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Constitution","content":"unwritten; partly statutes, partly common law and practice","ordinal":45,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/je.html#field:45","country":"JE","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Legal system","content":"English law and local statute; justice is administered by the Royal Court","ordinal":46,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/je.html#field:46","country":"JE","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Suffrage","content":"NA years of age; universal adult","ordinal":47,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/je.html#field:47","country":"JE","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Executive branch","content":"chief of state: Queen ELIZABETH II (since 6 February 1952)\n\nhead of government: Lieutenant Governor Andrew RIDGEWAY (since 14 June 2006); Bailiff Philip Martin BAILHACHE (since February 1995)\n\ncabinet: committees appointed by the Assembly of the States\n\nelections: none; the monarch is hereditary; lieutenant governor and bailiff appointed by the monarch","ordinal":48,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/je.html#field:48","country":"JE","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Legislative branch","content":"unicameral Assembly of the States (55 voting members - 12 senators (elected for six-year terms), 12 constables or heads of parishes (elected for three-year terms), 29 deputies (elected for three-year terms); the bailiff and the deputy bailiff; and three non-voting members - the Dean of Jersey, the Attorney General, and the Solicitor General all appointed by the monarch)\n\nelections: last held NA (next to be held NA); note - on 23 November 2005, 29 deputies, independents, were elected\n\nelection results: percent of vote - NA; seats - independents 55","ordinal":49,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/je.html#field:49","country":"JE","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Judicial branch","content":"Royal Court (judges elected by an electoral college and the bailiff)","ordinal":50,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/je.html#field:50","country":"JE","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Political parties and leaders","content":"none; all independents","ordinal":51,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/je.html#field:51","country":"JE","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Political pressure groups and leaders","content":"none","ordinal":52,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/je.html#field:52","country":"JE","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Diplomatic representation in the US","content":"none (British crown dependency)","ordinal":53,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/je.html#field:53","country":"JE","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Diplomatic representation from the US","content":"none (British crown dependency)","ordinal":54,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/je.html#field:54","country":"JE","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Flag description","content":"white with a diagonal red cross extending to the corners of the flag; in the upper quadrant, surmounted by a yellow crown, a red shield with the three lions of England in yellow","ordinal":55,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/je.html#field:55","country":"JE","edition_year":2006},{"category":"economy","label":"Economy - overview","content":"Jersey's economy is based on international financial services, agriculture, and tourism. In 1996, the finance sector accounted for about 60% of the island's output. Potatoes, cauliflower, tomatoes, and especially flowers are important export crops, shipped mostly to the UK. The Jersey breed of dairy cattle is known worldwide and represents an important export income earner. Milk products go to the UK and other EU countries. Tourism accounts for 24% of GDP. In recent years, the government has encouraged light industry to locate in Jersey, with the result that an electronics industry has developed alongside the traditional manufacturing of knitwear. All raw material and energy requirements are imported, as well as a large share of Jersey's food needs. Light taxes and death duties make the island a popular tax haven. Living standards come close to those of the UK.","ordinal":56,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/je.html#field:56","country":"JE","edition_year":2006},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP (purchasing power parity)","content":"$3.6 billion (2003 est.)","ordinal":57,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/je.html#field:57","country":"JE","edition_year":2006},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP (official exchange rate)","content":"NA","ordinal":58,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/je.html#field:58","country":"JE","edition_year":2006},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP - real growth rate","content":"NA%","ordinal":59,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/je.html#field:59","country":"JE","edition_year":2006},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP - per capita (PPP)","content":"$40,000 (2003 est.)","ordinal":60,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/je.html#field:60","country":"JE","edition_year":2006},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP - composition by sector","content":"agriculture: 5%\n\nindustry: 2%\n\nservices: 93% (1996)","ordinal":61,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/je.html#field:61","country":"JE","edition_year":2006},{"category":"economy","label":"Labor force","content":"52,790 (2004)","ordinal":62,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/je.html#field:62","country":"JE","edition_year":2006},{"category":"economy","label":"Unemployment rate","content":"0.9% (2004 est.)","ordinal":63,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/je.html#field:63","country":"JE","edition_year":2006},{"category":"economy","label":"Population below poverty line","content":"NA%","ordinal":64,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/je.html#field:64","country":"JE","edition_year":2006},{"category":"economy","label":"Hou